      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 0,
      "outputTokens": 0,
      "costUsd": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "Here are the finance phrases to look for. The same amount added each period means an arithmetic model, a straight line. The same percentage of the current amount means a geometric model, multiplying by one plus r each period. Equal end-of-period deposits into an account that starts at zero add up to a geometric series, so that's an annuity, with future value M times one plus r to the n, minus one, all over r. And equal repayments on a loan, where interest is charged on the balance, give the loan model, with the balance zero when it's paid off. In every one, r is the rate for one period, and n counts the periods. Which model does \"can afford a repayment each month\" point to? Think for three seconds. It's a loan with equal repayments."
    },
