      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 0,
      "outputTokens": 0,
      "costUsd": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "So here's that question. A buyer can afford two thousand eight hundred dollars a month, at four point eight per cent a year, compounded monthly, for twenty-five years. What's the most they can borrow? Per month, r is point zero zero four, and n is three hundred. The loan is paid off after the last repayment, so set the balance after three hundred months to zero. The unknown this time is P, the amount borrowed. Move the repayments' part to the other side and divide, and P is about four hundred and eighty-eight thousand, six hundred and fifty-eight dollars, seventy-nine. Because it's a maximum, round down, to seventy-eight cents, so the repayments are sure to clear it. Multiplying two thousand eight hundred by three hundred is the classic slip. That's the total repaid, including all the interest."
