      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 0,
      "outputTokens": 0,
      "costUsd": 0,
      "pronunciationText": "One more pair. In the first question, a spinner lands on one, two, three or four, with probability k x. In the second, X is a choc chip's distance from the centre of a cookie, in centimetres, and it has density k x, from zero to four. Same rule, but is k the same? For the list, the four probabilities add to one. That's k plus two k plus three k plus four k, which is ten k, so k is one tenth. For the density, the area under k x from zero to four is one. That's a triangle, half of four times four k, which is eight k, so k is one eighth, the cookie's density from the earlier video. A sum of bars and an area under a line are different totals, so they give different values of k."
    },
