      "pronunciationText": "Equal end-of-year deposits, starting from zero, make an annuity. The last one goes in at the end, so it earns nothing yet. So the value is two thousand, times one point zero five to the ten, minus one, all over point zero five. That's about twenty-five thousand, one hundred and fifty-five dollars, seventy-nine. Thirty-two thousand, five hundred and seventy-seven dollars, eighty-nine is wrong. It treats all ten deposits as if they went in at the start."
